break :--> stop the iteration or termination of the loop.
example7: write a tcl prm to print all the numbers from 1 to 100. and break when its in 70's.


for {set a 1} {$a <= 100} {incr a 1} {

if {$a / 10 == 7} {
break
}
puts $a
}


continue : -->skip current iteration and continue.

example 8: write a tcl prm to print all the num from 1 to 100 and skip whn it is in 70's

for {set a 1} {$a <= 100} {incr a 1} {

if {$a / 10 == 7} {
continue
}
puts $a
}



