-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What is a string in tcl?
	String is sequence of the char.
	in TCL string is enclosed double quotes ("")
	string contains in TCL char,numbers, special char.

How to define the string in the TCL?

set a "this is tcl class"
puts $a

In TCL, we have some built in srting operators:

1. string length:
It is used to find the length of the string including spaces.

example

	set a "this is tcl class"
	set b [string length $a ]
		puts $a
	puts "the lenth of the string is: $b"

2. string reverse:
It is used to reverse the string.
Example:
	set a "this is tcl class"
	set b [string reverse $a ]
	puts $a
	puts $b

3. string compare:
Compares two strings lexicographically and returns -1 if the first string is less than the second. 0 if they are equal, and 1 if first string is greater than the second.

example
	set a "this is tcl class"
	set c "this is tcl class"
	set b [string compare $a $c ]
	puts $b

4. String index :
	It is used to return the character at the index.
example: 
		set a "this is tcl class"
		puts $a
		set b [string index $a 15]
		puts $b

5. string range:
It is used to access the consecutive characters in the string.

example:
		set a "this is tcl class"
		puts $a
		set b [string range $a 1 15]
		puts $b

example2:
		set a "this is tcl class"
		puts $a
		set b [string range $a 1 end]
		puts $b


6. string tolower:
It is used to convert the upper case into lower case:

example:
		set a "THIS IS TCL CLASS"
		set b [string tolower $a]
		puts $a
		puts $b



		set a "THIS IS TCL CLASS"
		set b [string tolower $a 5 end ]
		puts $a
		puts $b

7. string toupper:
It is used to covert the lower case into upper case:
example:
		set a "this is tcl class"
		set b [string toupper $a]
		puts $a
		puts $b

		set a "this is tcl class"
		set b [string toupper $a 5 end]
		puts $a
		puts $b

8. String append:
It is used to add / append the string at the end of the existing srting.

example:
		set a "this is tcl class"
		puts $a
		append a " tommo no tcl class"
		puts $a


9. String trim:
It is used to remove spaces or specific characters at both ends of the string.

example:
		set a "   this is tcl class          "
		puts $a
		set b [string trim $a]
		puts $b

		set a "#####this is tcl class########"
		puts $a
		set b [string trim $a "#"]
		puts $b

		set a "$$$$ this is tcl class###"
		puts $a
		set b [string trim $a "# $ " ]
		puts $b

10. String trimleft:
It is used to trims the left of the begining of the string.

example:
		set a "     this is tcl clas"
		puts $a
		set b [string trimleft $a]
		puts $b

		set a "this is tcl class"
		puts $a
		set b "this"
		set c [string trimleft $a $b]
		puts $c

11. String trimright:

It is used to trims the right of the begining of the string.

example:
		set a "this is tcl class     "
		puts $a
		set c [string trimright $a " as"]
		puts $c
	
		set a "this is tcl class     "
		puts $a
		set c [string trimright $a]
		puts $c

12. String first:

It will search for exact match occurences string 1 in string 2 and returns the number of the charcters before matching, if it is not found it return -1.

example:
		set a "hello world"
		puts $a
		set b [string first "world" $a]
		puts $b

		set a "hello world"
		puts $a
		set b [string first "l" $a 9 ]
		puts $b


13.string last:

If we give any charector it will try to match that charector from last to the first of the string.

It is used to find the last occurence of a substring with in a string.

example:
		set a "this is tcl class"
		puts $a
		set b [string last "l" $a]
		puts $b


		

14. String wordstart:
It is used to return the index numbers of the 1st charector of the word cantaning the index number wwhich we are given:	

example:
		set a "this is tcl class"
		puts $a
		set b [string wordstart $a 14]
		puts $b

		
		set a "this is tcl class"
		puts $a
		set b [string wordstart $a 6 ]
		puts $b


15. String wordend:

It is used to return the index of the last charactor index in tha word contaning the charactor:

example:
		set a "this is tcl class"
		puts $a
		set b [string wordend $a 12 ]
		puts $b



16. String equal:

It is used to compare the two strings to determine if they are equal. if they are equal it returns 1 else returns as a 0.

example:

	set a "hello"
		set b "hello"
		set c [string equal $a $b]
		puts $c

		set a "hello"
		set b "hello"
		if {[string equal $a $b]} {
		puts "two strings are equal "
		} else {
		puts "two strings are not equal"
		}


17. String is :
It is used to test whether a given strings meets a certain criteria.

		
set a "HELLO"
set b [string is alpha $a]
puts $b

if {[string is alpha $a]} {
puts "$a contains only the alphabetic charector"
} else {
puts "$a does not contains only alphabetic charactors"
}


set a "12345"
set b [string is digit $a]
puts $b

if {[string is digit $a]} {
puts "$a contains only the digit charector"
} else {
puts "$a does not contains only digit charactors"
}


18. String match:

It is used to perform pattern maching on the string.

set a "hello world"
puts $a
set b [string match $a "world"]
puts $b

set a "hello world"
puts $a
if {[string match "hello world" $a]} {
puts "$a pattern matched"
} else {
puts "$a pattern does not match "
}
 

19. String map:

In Tcl, string map is a command is used to replace occurences of one or mpore substrings in a string with a specified replacement string. The basic syntax of string map is :

set str "the quick brown fox jump over the lazy dog."
set newstr [string map {quick fast brown red fox dog} $str]
puts $newstr

set str "the quick brown fox jump over the lazy dog."
puts $str
set newstr [string map {quick fast brown red fox dog} $str]
puts $newstr
set a [string map {" " "#"} $str]
puts $a


20. String replace:
In tcl, string replace is a command that is used to replace a portion of a string with a specified replacement string.

et str "the quick brown fox jump over the lazy dog."
puts $str
set newstr [string replace $str 4 8 "slow"]
puts $newstr



21. String cat :
In Tcl, string cat is a command that concatenates one or more strings together into a single string.

set a "good morning everyone"
puts $a
set b " this is tcl class"
puts $b

set c [string cat $a $b]
puts $c



22. String repeat:
In Tcl, string repeat is a command that is used to repeat a string a specified number of times.


set str "hello "
set r_str [string repeat $str 5]
puts $r_str



23. String Join:

In Tcl, string join is a command that is used to concatenate a list of strings into a single string, with a specified separator between each string.


set a {maneesh moulali narendra}
set c [join $a ","]
puts $c


24. String format:

In Tcl, string format is a command that is used to create a formated string based on a format string and a list of values.


