LIST:

In TCL, a list is a collection of values, typically strings or numbers, that are stored as a single value. Lists are represented as a series of elements separated by white space or brackets.


set a {1 2 3 4 5 5}
puts $a

list in the TCL:
list is collection of items or elements which are in orderd.
list is a one of the basic data type in tcl.
list contains elements of any type.
list can allow to create a list in the list.


how to create a list in tcl:

set a "1 2 3 4"
set a {1 2 3 4}
set a [list 1 2 3 4]


built in function of the list.
1. 	llength
2. 	lindex
3. 	lrange
4. 	linsert
5. 	lreplace
6. 	lassign
7. 	lappend
8. 	lset
9. 	split
10. concat

11. lsort
12. lsearch
13. lmap



1. llength

it is used to find the length of the list.

set a [list 1 2 3 4 5 6 6 7 8]
puts $a
set b [llength $a]
puts "length of the list is: $b"


2. lindex:
it is used to access the element of the list.

set a [list 1 2 3 4 5 6 6 7 8 hello]
puts $a
set b [lindex $a 9]
puts $b

set a [list [list 1 2 3 4 5 6 6 7 8] [list apple banana mango]]
puts $a
set b [lindex $a 0 1]
puts $b

3. lrange:
It is uded to access the consecutive elements in the list.
set a {1 2 34 56 3 4 5 67}
set c [lrange $a 2 4]
puts $c


4. linsert:
It is used to insert the element in the list

set a {1 2 34 56 3 4 5 67}
puts $a
set c [linsert $a 0 hello good morning 80]
puts $c
set d [lindex $c 0]
puts $d

5. lreplace:
It is used to replace the elements at particular element.

set a "apple banana mango grapes"
puts $a
set b [lreplace $a 0 0 orenge] (0 0 range)
puts $b

6.lassign:
It is used to assign the elements of the list into variables which we mentioned.

set a [list red green white blue grey]
puts $a
lassign $a b c d e f 
puts $b
puts $c
puts $d
puts $e
puts $f

